  Some of the most robust work has been done on personal networks, sometimes implicating ethnic or racial homophily \smallcite{gal_language_1979, stoessel_investigating_2002, fridland_network_2003, kirke_when_2005, li_two-step_2000, sharma_scalar_2017, wong_new_2010}
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item Results $\to$ High minority homophily leads to greater use of minority languages or features associated with minority groups
    \item A dearth of examinations of Louisiana, however
  \end{enumerate}
